;; Reviewed 2026-10-08 (written by Claude, from the design, the MACRO
;; manual, the VAX's listing and the debugger runs; for the user's
;; review). Why this is right:
;; - ABS(x) moves x to the result, then BGEQ over MNEGx: MOVx sets N when
;;   x is negative (MACRO 9-24), so only a negative x is negated; where x
;;   is the result already, TSTx sets N instead. MNEG of the most negative
;;   value is that value with V set (9-23), the trap being off (section
;;   7), so ABS(-128) as a SHORTINT is -128, as poc's wrapping arithmetic
;;   promises (run-values). A HUGEINT tests its high longword and is
;;   negated as -x is: MNEGL of each longword, then SBWC #0 for the borrow.
;; - ODD(x) is BICB3 #254, x, result: the low bit of x's low byte, a
;;   BOOLEAN 0 or 1. A word, longword or HUGEINT location is read as a byte
;;   where it is, the VAX being little-endian; an element in index mode,
;;   words[k], is moved to a register first, since index mode scales by
;;   the instruction's operand size (section 8).
;; - CHR(x) is CVTWB, or CVTLB of a HUGEINT's low longword: the low byte, a
;;   longer integer converted to a shorter one being truncated, with V set
;;   on overflow (9-16), which traps only with IV set. Without
;;   -range-checks nothing is checked, as on LLVM.
;; - ORD of a CHAR is MOVZBW, zero-extended to an INTEGER (16 bits under
;;   -O2, the VAX target's model): ORD(200X) is 200. ORD of a SET is
;;   CVTLW, its low word, as LLVM truncates it.
;; - CAP(x) subtracts 32 when x is 97 to 122, "a" to "z", by unsigned
;;   compares, as for every CHAR; other characters are left, as on LLVM.
;; - HALT(7) is PUSHL #7 and CALLS #1, G^POC_HALT, poc's runtime routine,
;;   declared .EXTERNAL: it ends the program, n being its status; Phase 16
;;   writes it and decides what VMS sees, as for POC_TRAP (section 9). The
;;   debugger runs link a stand-in that keeps the code (run-halt).
;; - LEN(words) is the constant 4, MOVW #4, since LEN of a fixed array is
;;   folded. In the body ABS and CAP write the variable itself, as an
;;   assignment's last operation does when as wide: c := CAP(c) changes c
;;   in place.
;; - A function's value is returned in R0 as a longword (CVTBL, CVTWL,
;;   MOVZBL), and a HUGEINT value parameter is copied on entry, both as in
;;   step 5.
; VaxPredeclared, written by poc (doc/developer/vax-macro32-backend.md)
	.TITLE	VAXPREDECLARED
	.IDENT	/897311a6a8516e41/
	.PSECT	POC_CODE,  PIC,SHR,NOWRT,EXE,LONG
	.PSECT	POC_CONST, PIC,SHR,NOWRT,NOEXE,QUAD
	.PSECT	POC_DATA,  NOPIC,NOSHR,WRT,NOEXE,QUAD

; set once the module has been initialised
	.PSECT	POC_DATA
L_INITIALISED:
	.BLKB	1

; the module's variables
